{"id":"054f5df77a4bd18d","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration.md","title":"ZFC Two Step Iteration","display":"df-zfc-two-step-iteration — ZFC Two Step Iteration","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration","aliases":["58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration"],"display":"df-zfc-two-step-iteration — ZFC Two Step Iteration","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-forcing-notion.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md]]","[[../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-name.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-two-step-iteration</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-two-step-iteration — ZFC Two Step Iteration"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d413862f4ab047c8\" href=\"?note=d413862f4ab047c8\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-forcing-notion.md\">../batch13/58-df-forcing-notion.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"911508dbd8495663\" href=\"?note=911508dbd8495663\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"a9132c2c1a18acd1\" href=\"?note=a9132c2c1a18acd1\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model.md\">../batch19/58-df-zfc-transitive-model.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ec28b62254928d73\" href=\"?note=ec28b62254928d73\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-name.md\">../batch07/58-df-name.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P=\\langle P,\\preccurlyeq_P,1_P\\rangle\">\\(\\mathbb P=\\langle P,\\preccurlyeq_P,1_P\\rangle\\)</span> (first forcing notion)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dot{\\mathbb Q}=\\langle\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot 1_Q\\rangle\">\\(\\dot{\\mathbb Q}=\\langle\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot 1_Q\\rangle\\)</span> (a <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P\">\\(\\mathbb P\\)</span>-name)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\\in V\">\\(M\\in V\\)</span> (transitive set ground model containing the forcing data)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span> (iteration-forcing candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ForcingNotion}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ForcingNotion}_S\\)</span> (forcing-notion predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d413862f4ab047c8\" href=\"?note=d413862f4ab047c8\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-forcing-notion\">../batch13/58-df-forcing-notion</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Name}\">\\(\\mathrm{Name}\\)</span> (ground-model and forcing-name predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\">\\(\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\\)</span> is the displayed <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{\\in\\}\">\\(\\{\\in\\}\\)</span>-formula saying that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_1\">\\(v_1\\)</span> is a partial order on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0\">\\(v_0\\)</span> with greatest element <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_2\">\\(v_2\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_\\in(v_0,v_1)\">\\(\\theta_\\in(v_0,v_1)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_{\\leq}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\">\\(\\theta_{\\leq}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\\)</span> abbreviate <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0\\in v_1\">\\(v_0\\in v_1\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle v_0,v_1\\rangle\\in v_2\">\\(\\langle v_0,v_1\\rangle\\in v_2\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}\\urcorner,\\ulcorner\\theta_\\in\\urcorner,\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\leq}\\urcorner\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\">\\(\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}\\urcorner,\\ulcorner\\theta_\\in\\urcorner,\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\leq}\\urcorner\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_\\in)\\)</span> are their set codes under the syntax constructors of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\)</span> (six-argument forcing relation, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"911508dbd8495663\" href=\"?note=911508dbd8495663\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-zfc-forcing-relation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TwoStepIteration}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{TwoStepIteration}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}two\\text{-}step\\text{-}iteration\\text{-}formulae}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\\leftrightarrow\nv_1\\subseteq v_0\\times v_0\n\\land\\forall x\\in v_0\\;(\\langle x,x\\rangle\\in v_1)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall x,y,z\\in v_0\\;((\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in v_1\\land\\langle y,z\\rangle\\in v_1)\n\\to\\langle x,z\\rangle\\in v_1)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall x,y\\in v_0\\;((\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in v_1\\land\\langle y,x\\rangle\\in v_1)\\to x=y)\n\\land v_2\\in v_0\n\\land\\forall x\\in v_0\\;(\\langle x,v_2\\rangle\\in v_1),\\\\\n&amp;\\theta_\\in(v_0,v_1)\\leftrightarrow v_0\\in v_1,\\\\\n&amp;\\theta_{\\leq}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\\leftrightarrow\\langle v_0,v_1\\rangle\\in v_2.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}two\\text{-}step\\text{-}iteration\\text{-}formulae}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\\leftrightarrow\nv_1\\subseteq v_0\\times v_0\n\\land\\forall x\\in v_0\\;(\\langle x,x\\rangle\\in v_1)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall x,y,z\\in v_0\\;((\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in v_1\\land\\langle y,z\\rangle\\in v_1)\n\\to\\langle x,z\\rangle\\in v_1)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall x,y\\in v_0\\;((\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in v_1\\land\\langle y,x\\rangle\\in v_1)\\to x=y)\n\\land v_2\\in v_0\n\\land\\forall x\\in v_0\\;(\\langle x,v_2\\rangle\\in v_1),\\\\\n&amp;\\theta_\\in(v_0,v_1)\\leftrightarrow v_0\\in v_1,\\\\\n&amp;\\theta_{\\leq}(v_0,v_1,v_2)\\leftrightarrow\\langle v_0,v_1\\rangle\\in v_2.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}two\\text{-}step\\text{-}iteration}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TwoStepIteration}_S(\\mathbb R,M,\\mathbb P,\\dot{\\mathbb Q})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists P,\\preccurlyeq_P,1_P,C,\\preccurlyeq_R,1_R,\n\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot 1_Q\\;\n\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(M)\n\\land\\mathbb P,\\dot{\\mathbb Q}\\in M\n\\land\n\\mathbb P=\\langle P,\\preccurlyeq_P,1_P\\rangle\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ForcingNotion}_S(\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\n\\dot{\\mathbb Q}\n=\\langle\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot 1_Q\\rangle\n\\land\n\\forall\\sigma\\in\\{\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot1_Q\\}\\;\n(\\sigma\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\sigma,P))\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\n(M,1_P,\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}\\urcorner,\n\\langle\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot1_Q\\rangle,P,\\preccurlyeq_P)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\n\\mathbb R=\\langle C,\\preccurlyeq_R,1_R\\rangle\n\\land\nC=\n\\left\\{\n\\langle p,\\dot q\\rangle:\np\\in P\n\\land\\dot q\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\dot q,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\n(M,p,\\ulcorner\\theta_\\in\\urcorner,\\langle\\dot q,\\dot Q\\rangle,P,\\preccurlyeq_P)\n\\right\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\n\\forall\\langle p,\\dot q\\rangle,\n\\langle p&#39;,\\dot q&#39;\\rangle\\in C\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\langle p,\\dot q\\rangle\n\\preccurlyeq_R\n\\langle p&#39;,\\dot q&#39;\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\qquad\\leftrightarrow\np\\preccurlyeq_P p&#39;\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\n(M,p,\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\leq}\\urcorner,\n\\langle\\dot q,\\dot q&#39;,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q\\rangle,P,\\preccurlyeq_P)\n\\Bigr)\n\\land\n1_R=\\langle1_P,\\dot1_Q\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{ForcingNotion}_S(\\mathbb R)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}two\\text{-}step\\text{-}iteration}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TwoStepIteration}_S(\\mathbb R,M,\\mathbb P,\\dot{\\mathbb Q})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists P,\\preccurlyeq_P,1_P,C,\\preccurlyeq_R,1_R,\n\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot 1_Q\\;\n\\Bigl[\n\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(M)\n\\land\\mathbb P,\\dot{\\mathbb Q}\\in M\n\\land\n\\mathbb P=\\langle P,\\preccurlyeq_P,1_P\\rangle\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ForcingNotion}_S(\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\n\\dot{\\mathbb Q}\n=\\langle\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot 1_Q\\rangle\n\\land\n\\forall\\sigma\\in\\{\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot1_Q\\}\\;\n(\\sigma\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\sigma,P))\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\n(M,1_P,\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\mathrm{fn}}\\urcorner,\n\\langle\\dot Q,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q,\\dot1_Q\\rangle,P,\\preccurlyeq_P)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\n\\mathbb R=\\langle C,\\preccurlyeq_R,1_R\\rangle\n\\land\nC=\n\\left\\{\n\\langle p,\\dot q\\rangle:\np\\in P\n\\land\\dot q\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\dot q,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\n(M,p,\\ulcorner\\theta_\\in\\urcorner,\\langle\\dot q,\\dot Q\\rangle,P,\\preccurlyeq_P)\n\\right\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\n\\forall\\langle p,\\dot q\\rangle,\n\\langle p&#39;,\\dot q&#39;\\rangle\\in C\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\langle p,\\dot q\\rangle\n\\preccurlyeq_R\n\\langle p&#39;,\\dot q&#39;\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\qquad\\leftrightarrow\np\\preccurlyeq_P p&#39;\n\\land\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\n(M,p,\\ulcorner\\theta_{\\leq}\\urcorner,\n\\langle\\dot q,\\dot q&#39;,\\dot{\\preccurlyeq}_Q\\rangle,P,\\preccurlyeq_P)\n\\Bigr)\n\\land\n1_R=\\langle1_P,\\dot1_Q\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{ForcingNotion}_S(\\mathbb R)\n\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The three forcing formulae and their quotation codes are fixed by the definition itself, so the four-argument predicate has no free meta-level formula-code parameters. The second coordinate is required to be a genuine ground-model <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>-name.</li>\n<li>The result is the full forcing structure with carrier, order, and top condition, and it is checked again by the forcing-notion predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAn